1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,900
three.ws gives your AI a body: a 3D avatar, a voice and a persona.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,900
Describe an object in one sentence.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,900
Forge builds it on the free lane. No account needed.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,900
A textured 3D model from that one prompt.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,900
Orbit it, download it as GLB, or place it in a scene.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,900
Open any GLB or glTF in the three.ws viewer, right in the browser.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,400
Give an avatar a persona and skills, and it becomes an agent.

8
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:37,900
Every agent has a public page anyone can visit and chat with.

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,900
In Microsoft Teams, the three.ws tab lists agents and what each one did today.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,900
Share an agent into a chat as an Adaptive Card with its live numbers.

11
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:57,900
In Visual Studio Code, ask GitHub Copilot to make and preview 3D models with three.ws.

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:03,900
three.ws is live on Microsoft Marketplace. Start free at three.ws.
